    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 from INV-nular's 09-03 entry (measurement 0012's entire VACUOUS class) and sized on six Go repositories. This is the WRITE-side twin of INV-bagok / INV-zumin class (b) and of WI-vutav's read rows: a primitive whose FIRST argument is the stream decides its boundary by what that stream is, and go.yaml declares one fixed boundary for each.\n\nTHE ROWS. go.yaml: io.WriteString -> fs_write only (no boundary_ruling; gocryptfs:untrusted-input-no-host-fs:0 writes to cmd.StdinPipe() -- a pipe to a child -- and was reported as a host-filesystem crossing, 0012 VACUOUS:KIND-MISDECLARED). fmt.Fprint/Fprintf/Fprintln -> logging only (\"Console output\") though the first argument is any io.Writer. io.Copy -> fs_read only (its SOURCE), with the destination unrepresented.\n\nSIZED (grep, six repos: alertmanager beads caddy cert-manager cilium jaeger): 6,373 calls -- fmt.Fprintf 2,897, io.Copy 2,537, Fprintln 529, Fprint 293, io.WriteString 117. First-argument shapes: os.Stdout/os.Stderr 1,695; &buf / &sb (an in-memory buffer by address) 2,637; a bare identifier 1,620 (very often an http.ResponseWriter or io.Writer PARAMETER); a field/chain 388; a call 32. Every one of those is classified today as fs_write (WriteString) or logging (Fprint*), whatever the writer.\n\nWHAT EXISTS TO REUSE, all shipped: the read-side seam (_target_kind_discriminated_keys / _narrow_by_target_kind / read_boundary_for_target_kind, WI-lipis), the go argument classifier with one binding hop taken at the wrapper's line (_go_handle_kind_from_argument_text, WI-vutav), TaintSource.requires_target_kind, and the site-C wrapper stamp (_go_wrapped_handle_kind) keyed on _GO_HANDLE_WRAPPERS.\n\nDESIGN (decided from the record; the one collision found is resolved by the later, cross-language ruling):\n  1. Vocabulary. write_boundary_for_target_kind: host_path -> fs_write; std_stream -> logging (WI-dutah, shipped 05-13 for c/rust/js/elixir; the c.yaml unistd.write ipc_send note \"write(STDOUT_FILENO)\" is the stale sibling and is disclosed here, not followed); in_memory / null_device -> crosses nothing (existing); NEW `pipe` -> ipc_send (cmd.StdinPipe/StdoutPipe/StderrPipe, io.Pipe, os.Pipe); NEW `net_stream` -> net_send, and on the READ side net_stream -> net_recv, which is exactly the value INV-bagok says is missing for its NETWORK CASE (bufio.NewScanner(conn)). The vocabulary gate test_widening_the_vocabulary_moves_the_source_side_too must be satisfied on both sides.\n  2. Seam. _target_kind_discriminated_keys generalises from \"two or more READ boundaries\" to \"two or more boundaries of ONE direction\"; _narrow_by_target_kind / resolve_target_kind_across_sites take the direction from the candidate rows; TaintSink gains requires_target_kind mirroring the source side so an fs_write sink does not fire on a stamped pipe write.\n  3. Rows. io.WriteString and fmt.Fprint* declared under fs_write + ipc_send + net_send + logging, boundary_ruling call_site_undecidable, abstains_to = today's answer (fs_write / logging) so an unstamped call classifies exactly as before (INV-fatok). io.Copy is DEFERRED: fs_read + fs_write is a mode-discriminated pair and would enter the mode seam; disclose on the row, file separately if the measurement says it matters.\n  4. Stamp. _GO_HANDLE_WRAPPERS becomes a (module, callee) -> argument-index table so io.WriteString / fmt.Fprint* stamp from argument 0 at the existing site; the classifier learns os.Stdout/os.Stderr (std_stream), the pipe producers, and TYPE-based kinds for a typed receiver or parameter through var_types: *bytes.Buffer / *strings.Builder -> in_memory (the &buf shape, 2,637 sites), http.ResponseWriter / net.Conn / *tls.Conn -> net_stream, io.Writer / *os.File -> abstain (an os.File may be stdout, a file, or a pipe).\n  5. Measure. A/B on the six repos, arm A finished before any edit, every moved row read back with the writer's binding recovered from source; report the repo where nothing moved. The removal direction is live here (a sink that stops firing is a false-all-clear risk), so every row that LOSES a sink must be read back individually (WI-zozun's `removed>0` rule).\n\nNOT THIS ITEM: c's sys/socket send/sendto/sendmsg (AF_UNIX vs AF_INET), filed as a sibling. verify_claims has no consumer of boundary_ruling (grep: none); the seam, not the declaration, is what changes a verdict."  # 78ee
    fields: {}  # 78ee
