  clock: 4  # e882
  nonce: e882  # e882
  message: "DONE in PR #743. Shipped as designed on the item, with two changes to the design forced by measurement, both disclosed:\n\nWHAT LANDED. go.yaml: io.WriteString and fmt.Fprint/Fprintln/Fprintf dual under fs_write / ipc_send / net_send / logging, call_site_undecidable, abstains_to = today's answer (fs_write / logging); Print* stay single-row. Vocabulary: `pipe` (cmd.Std*Pipe, os.Pipe) and `net_stream` (a connection, a response writer); `_WRITE_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY` (host_path->fs_write, std_stream->logging per WI-dutah, pipe->ipc_send, net_stream->net_send); the read map gained pipe->ipc_recv and net_stream->net_recv and the bufio constructors + Reader/Scanner reads gained their net_recv rows (the row INV-bagok withheld until this kind existed). Seam: `_target_kind_gated_directions` -- \"two or more boundaries of ONE direction\" -- refuses a primitive gated in both at load; `_narrow_by_target_kind` and `resolve_target_kind_across_sites(direction=)` resolve per direction; io.Copy DEFERRED on its row (a mode pair). Taint: TaintSink.requires_target_kind, resolved in the write direction. go.py: `_GO_TARGET_ARGUMENT_INDEX` (call -> target argument), one classifier for the wrapper site, the write site and WI-vutav's receiver hop: inline producers, a table member followed into its own target (tabwriter.NewWriter / bufio.NewWriter / io.LimitReader), identifier through last binding (3 hops), declared TYPE via var_types (bytes.Buffer / strings.Builder -> in_memory; net.Conn / *tls.Conn / http.ResponseWriter -> net_stream; io.Writer, *os.File abstain).\n\nDESIGN CHANGE 1 (INV-minol, filed and fixed here). The item said \"TaintSink gains requires_target_kind mirroring the source side\". Mirroring it verbatim would have deleted every unstamped io.WriteString sink, because the source side's abstention admits only unconditional entries -- and, measured, that already deletes every unstamped bufio.NewScanner SOURCE today. Both entry kinds now carry `abstention_fallback`, set from the classifier's own fallback row.\n\nDESIGN CHANGE 2. The `_GO_HANDLE_WRAPPERS -> arg-index table` also carries the non-transferring wrappers (tabwriter.NewWriter, bufio.NewWriter, io.LimitReader) so a local bound to one is followed into ITS target: the largest resolvable write shape on the corpus (~210 sites) was `tw := tabwriter.NewWriter(os.Stdout, ...)` / `bw := bufio.NewWriter(f)`, which the item's four steps did not name.\n\nMEASURED (six repos: alertmanager beads caddy cert-manager cilium jaeger; arm A finished before any edit; call-edge counts identical; ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/suhug_writes_09032026/): 1,948 Fprint*/io.WriteString call edges (the item's 6,373 was a grep over every callee named WriteString/Copy -- 435 are strings.Builder.WriteString and 2,537 \"io.Copy\" were mostly not io.Copy at all; the analyzer emits 56). 1,194 stamped (61.3%). 29 MOVED / 0 REMOVED; nothing moved in alertmanager, cert-manager, jaeger. Every moved row read back (ab_compare.out): 20 logging->fs_write are os.Create / os.OpenFile / os.CreateTemp handles or bufio.NewWriter over one; 8 logging->net_send are a net.Dial conn and http.ResponseWriter params; 1 fs_write->logging is caddy io.WriteString(os.Stdout, BrowseTemplate). 994 std_stream stamps keep logging. 169 rows lose their sink at the carry gate (non-crossing stamp): 96 strings.Builder, 32 bytes.Buffer, 15 hashes, 24 tabwriters over those -- each read back (noncrossing_rows.txt). ONE read-back is a known limitation: cilium pkg/k8s/client/testutils/fake.go:495 -- `out := s.LogWriter()` then `out = f` (os.OpenFile) inside an `if`; the last-binding rule has no branch reasoning and takes the file -> fs_write, keeping a sink in the wrong zone (safe direction). Filed as WI-kupam-kohun-banam-tijoj-zuguk-vutup-hafil-siduh.\n**Read side under the same tree** (`vutav_reads_09032026/bc_compare_readside.out`): 14 `bufio` rows gained a stamp -- caddy `httpredirectlistener.go:91` (`bufio.NewReader(c)`, a `net.Conn` from `Accept`; INV-bagok's own headline case) and alertmanager `tls_transport_test.go:226` (`var to net.Conn`) are now `net_stream` → `net_recv`; five constructors and their seven `Scan`/`Text` reads are `in_memory` (`&out` over a declared `bytes.Buffer`, `io.LimitReader(&compilerStderr, n)`, two `io.Pipe()` readers). 12 constructors remain unstamped and now MINT their declared `ipc_recv` fallback (INV-minol), each read back: 3 true untrusted inputs (alertmanager's TLS connection through a struct field, caddy's fastcgi response from `c.Do`, cilium's remote `ExecInPod` output), 8 `io.Reader` / `*os.File` / `io.ReadSeeker` parameters whose callers read files (a caddyfile, an env file, IPsec keys, `/proc` schedstat and mountinfo, a Prometheus dump) -- INV-bagok's accepted trade, now visible on the taint side as it always was on the boundary tagger -- and 1 behind a multi-line signature. The lever for the eight is typing a parameter through its CALLER, which is inter-procedural and not this item.\n\nDENOMINATOR (INV-nopoh, filed P1): on beads 578 of 1,331 fmt.Fprintf sites emit NO call edge -- inside package-level function literals (every cobra Run handler). No row can reach them; this item's reach is capped by it.\n\nNOT DONE / DISCLOSED: struct-field writers (166 sites: env.stdout, params.Writer) abstain -- field-chain target kinds would need `_resolve_field_chain`, not built; io.Writer / *bufio.Writer / *tabwriter.Writer parameters (321) abstain by design; cobra `cmd.OutOrStdout()` (34) abstains. Method-form write rows absent: os.File.WriteString (7), bufio.Writer.WriteString (10) -- filed as WI-nunab-tagom-nuzas-napif-lusak-ladoz-zogit-rafiv. WI-baran's landing zone is live: a c `write` stamped `pipe` selects the ipc sink (pinned)."  # e882
